%H A288030 <a href="/index/Rec#order_18">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (3,6,35,-7,15,-55,31,36,36,-124,0,-8,32,1,9,-2,-2,-1).
%F A288030 Empirical: a(n) = 3*a(n-1)+6*a(n-2)+35*a(n-3) -7*a(n-4)+15*a(n-5)-55*a(n-6) +31*a(n-7)+36*a(n-8)+36*a(n-9) -124*a(n-10)-8*a(n-12)+32*a(n-13) +a(n-14)+9*a(n-15)-2*a(n-16) -2*a(n-17)-a(n-18) for n >= 18.
%F A288030 Empirical g.f.: (1 - 2*x - 3*x^2 - 21*x^3 + 12*x^4 + 5*x^5 + 43*x^6 - 16*x^7 - 30*x^8 - 34*x^9 + 42*x^10 - 5*x^11 + 5*x^12 - 3*x^13 - x^14 - x^15)/(1 - 3*x - 6*x^2 - 35*x^3 + 7*x^4 - 15*x^5 + 55*x^6 - 31*x^7 - 36*x^8 - 36*x^9 + 124*x^10 + 8*x^12 - 32*x^13 - x^14 - 9*x^15 + 2*x^16 + 2*x^17 + x^18). - _Colin Barker_, Jun 16 2017
%F A288030 The above empirical formulas are correct. The sequence satisfies a recurrence of order (3^3 + 3^ceiling(3/2))/2 = 18. - _Andrew Howroyd_, Jul 29 2026
%t A288030 LinearRecurrence[{3, 6, 35, -7, 15, -55, 31, 36, 36, -124, 0, -8, 32, 1, 9, -2, -2, -1}, {1, 1, 6, 38, 190, 1021, 5494, 29042, 154772, 824695, 4386942, 23356322, 124344111, 661873859, 3523418150, 18756407661, 99845472493, 531509598443}, 25] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Jul 29 2026 *)
